hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"923","Narrated to me Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi, narrated to me Ismail bin Ulayya, narrated to me Ayyoub, H, and Mu’mal bin Hisham narrated to me, narrated to me Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw dirt in the direction of the mosque and rubbed it off, or he said: he rubbed it off. with his hand, then he approached the people, became angry with them, and said: “Indeed, God Almighty and Majestic kisses the face of any one of you in his prayer, so let no one snort before... his face in his prayer.”"
"924","We are Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Naseem, I am Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bakr Al-Barsani, Abu Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, that Shayth bin Rabi’i prayed next to Hudhayfah, and spit in his hands. Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from that. He said: “When a man begins his prayer, God faces him, and he does not turn away from Him until He turns away from Him, or an event occurs.”"
